    {
      "id": "BGM-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-binary-good-mass",
      "title": "The binary Gram mass is a four-variable local density",
      "statement": "At every good finite place the nonzero-length Gram-fibre mass of the binary coordinate lattice is the local density of Q(x)=xᵗBx/2 on four base-field coordinates. Its support is integral and its integral is one.",
      "hypotheses": "CM quadratic extension and a fixed basis over the base field, a nonsingular Hermitian plane, scalar Haar measure of unit integer-ring volume and the corresponding Gram-fibre measures. At the good places 2 and det B are units and B has integral entries.",
      "dependencies": [
        "BGM-04"
      ],
