    {
      "id": "BGM-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-binary-valuation-step",
      "title": "Scaling the imprimitive part gives a uniform binary mass bound",
      "statement": "For nonzero s of valuation at least two, its density equals the primitive contribution plus q⁻² times the density at s/π². Induction gives |gᵥ(s)−1|≤3/q for every nonzero integral target. Unit targets satisfy the sharper bound 1/q². These two estimates enter the global length average.",
      "hypotheses": "Same good-place assumptions. The identity concerns nonzero integral lengths and the unit-volume coordinate lattice, with π any uniformizer. The global length-average argument applies this calculation in the anisotropic binary case.",
      "dependencies": [
        "BGM-01",
        "BGM-02"
      ],
